<qti-assessment-item xmlns="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0" xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance" xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.imsglobal.org/xsd/imsqtiasi_v3p0 https://purl.imsglobal.org/spec/qti/v3p0/schema/xsd/imsqti_asiv3p0_v1p0.xsd" identifier="pcb-item-f405e06d3b10401aab26a3e7acd550b9" title="sat-c3-u24-dogma.html qc1" adaptive="true" time-dependent="false">
  <qti-response-declaration identifier="RESPONSE" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-correct-response><qti-value>C</qti-value></qti-correct-response>
  </qti-response-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="SCORE" cardinality="single" base-type="float"><qti-default-value><qti-value>0</qti-value></qti-default-value></qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="FEEDBACK" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier"/>
  <qti-outcome-declaration identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" cardinality="single" base-type="identifier">
    <qti-default-value><qti-value>show_interaction</qti-value></qti-default-value>
  </qti-outcome-declaration>
  <qti-item-body>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="show_interaction" outcome-identifier="INTERACTION_VISIBILITY" show-hide="show" class="qti-margin-0">
      <qti-content-body>
        <p>Which sentence uses &quot;dogma&quot; correctly?</p>
    <qti-choice-interaction response-identifier="RESPONSE" shuffle="true" max-choices="1">
      <qti-simple-choice identifier="A">Praised for her dogma, the moderator gave equal time to every viewpoint on the panel and carefully committed herself to none of them.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="B">The dogma that the cafeteria would drop pizza Fridays swept the school by lunchtime and was cheerfully debunked by two o&apos;clock.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="C">In Grandma&apos;s kitchen it was dogma that the sauce must never reach a boil; no one knew the reason, and no one dared to ask her.</qti-simple-choice><qti-simple-choice identifier="D">The committee&apos;s dogma was posted for public comment, every clause of it open to amendment before the final vote next spring.</qti-simple-choice>
    </qti-choice-interaction>
      </qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>

    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-A" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Dogma means beliefs laid down as unquestionable, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a moderator who commits to no position holds no fixed belief at all — even-handedness is the opposite habit.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-B" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Dogma means a standing belief handed down by authority, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a lunchtime story debunked by two o&apos;clock is a rumor — circulating news, checkable and checked, not a fixed principle.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-C" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Correct! Dogma means a belief laid down as unquestionably true, so it&apos;s the correct answer because the sauce rule is obeyed on Grandma&apos;s authority alone — no reason given, and no questioning allowed.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
    <qti-feedback-block identifier="FB-D" outcome-identifier="FEEDBACK" show-hide="show">
      <qti-content-body><p>Not quite! Dogma means principles closed to challenge, so it&apos;s not the correct choice here because a draft posted for comment, with every clause open to amendment, is the most questionable document there is.</p></qti-content-body>
    </qti-feedback-block>
  </qti-item-body>
  <qti-response-processing>
